Crowd sounds
------------
  - assets/sfx/city/crowd-walla.m4a (the street crowd's walla, wagmi/audio/city.js): cut and mixed from five
    takes of "GameSoundCon2024 Walla XY-AKG214-96k" (Freesound pack 42098) by ShangusBurger (Shane Vincent)
      https://freesound.org/people/ShangusBurger/packs/42098/
      Conference Room Walla American English 01            https://freesound.org/s/763895/
      Conference Room Walla American English 02            https://freesound.org/s/763896/
      Soft Conference Room Walla American English Library  https://freesound.org/s/763898/
      Sparse Chatter and Laughter                          https://freesound.org/s/763848/
      Coughs, Chatter and Laughs                           https://freesound.org/s/763851/
    dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). CC0 needs
    no credit; we give it anyway. Changed: resampled to 44.1 kHz; the room's reverb tail reduced; equalised to
    sound outdoors (high-passed at 150 Hz, the room's low boom and the voices' presence lowered, the top softened
    for distance); levelled; the stereo narrowed; three takes joined into a seamless 37.5 s loop with
    equal-power crossfades and the two sparse takes mixed under it; re-encoded to AAC.


Voices (assets/voice)
---------------------
  - Quant, Juno, Bagsy, Lev, Gears, Fiona, Wick and Fomo: synthesised with Qwen3-TTS by the Qwen team,
    Alibaba Cloud (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-TTS). Each voice was designed once with
    Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-VoiceDesign and every line cloned from it with Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-Base, using the
    mlx-community conversions (Apache-2.0) run with mlx-audio (MIT, https://github.com/Blaizzy/mlx-audio).
    The voices are invented: no real person's voice was used. Their reference clips are in
    wagmi/radio/build/tts/.
  - ZK (and any character not yet voiced): placeholders made with the macOS speech voices (the `say`
    command; ZK's through a voice changer made in code). They are meant to be replaced by recordings or
    synthesised voices like the others'. assets/voice/manifest.json records each line's source;
    docs/VOICE-LINES.md is the line sheet and says how to drop new voices in.